  "new_commit_message": "Maker Week: make firebase-apk-scanner report what the scan actually found (#374)\n\n* fix(firebase-apk-scanner): read the current report, keep it on nonzero exit, count vulnerabilities once\n\n- Step 3 ran `cat firebase_scan_*/scan_report.txt`, which also reads every\n  earlier scan in the directory, and took counts from the text report\n  although the reporting rule names scan_report.json. Read the JSON (and\n  text) report in the directory the scanner printed as `Results saved to:`.\n- scanner.sh exits 1 after writing its report when no APK could be tested,\n  which the \"if the scanner fails\" fallback read as a failure and started\n  manual live probes. Present a written report on any exit code; fall back\n  only when no report exists.\n- State the scanner's coverage limits (Cloud Functions in us-central1 only;\n  auth, functions and Remote Config for the first project and key only).\n- The per-APK \"APK IS VULNERABLE\" summary line used log_vuln, which counts\n  toward TOTAL_VULNS, so total_vulnerabilities was one too high for every\n  vulnerable APK. Log it with log_error. Documented output change.\n- Quote \"$ARGUMENTS\" so paths with spaces work.\n\ntests/test_scanner_reports.py runs the scanner with mocked apktool and curl\n(secure, vulnerable, no-config, failed) and checks the counts, the stale\ndirectory, and the SKILL.md guidance; two tests fail before this change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* perf(firebase-apk-scanner): load the manual-testing fallback only when needed\n\nMove \"Manual Testing (If Scanner Fails)\" word for word into\nreferences/manual-fallback.md and leave a two-line pointer: it is only\nneeded when the scanner wrote no report, but every run loaded it. Every\nother section is unchanged. Bump firebase-apk-scanner to 2.2.3.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: kz-tob <kara.zaffarano@trailofbits.com>",
